# DTF tier manifest: plugin-reload-ssrf  (artifact-keeper#4757, GHSA-r8fc-5fvw-rvh4)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-git (two stdlib-python git
# smart-HTTP servers serving one signed WASM plugin repository: an approved
# host at 172.16.<slot>.80 that AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS admits as a /32,
# and an internal host at .81 that nothing admits).
#
# THE BUG (#4757, fixed in 1.11.2 by #4761)
# POST /api/v1/plugins/{id}/reload re-cloned a git-sourced plugin's stored
# source_url through fetch_from_git -> clone_repository with no outbound-URL
# check. Install validates the URL once, so a source whose host later moved
# to (or started resolving to) a private, loopback or internal address was
# cloned from anyway: reload became a mapper of services reachable from the
# backend. The fix runs the same validate_outbound_url guard install uses
# before every re-fetch and refuses with install's 400 ("Plugin git URL IP
# '<ip>' is not allowed (private/internal network)", naming
# AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS for an address an operator can admit).
#
# THE ORACLE
#   * installs a signed plugin over the real API from http://plugin-src/...
#     (resolves to the approved host) and reloads it once to 2.0.0
#     (CONTROLS: the legitimate install and reload work on both images);
#   * re-points the `plugin-src` name to the internal host (the advisory's
#     DNS flip; the stored URL never changes) and reloads: FIXED = 400 naming
#     AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS, the internal host sees no request, the
#     version stays put. BASELINE = the internal host serves the clone and
#     the plugin is replaced from it;
#   * reloads plugins whose stored source names loopback (the backend's own
#     port), cloud metadata, a blocked service name and a file:// path:
#     FIXED = 400 from the guard and (loopback) no request in the backend's
#     own log. BASELINE = a clone attempt;
#   * CONTROLS on both images: install refuses the internal host; a reload
#     whose clone carries a bad or missing detached signature is refused by
#     the signing gate (PLUGINS_TRUSTED_PUBKEY) and leaves the version alone.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives a dozen admin API calls back to
# back; the base default (ON) is not what this tier is about.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-git"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
